-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Unser</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Automated segmentation of the corpus callosum in midsagittal brain magnetic resonance images</article-title><source><italic>Optical Engineering</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>39</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>924</fpage><lpage>935</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bueno</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Musse</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Heitz</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Armspach</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Three-dimensional segmentation of anatomical structures in MR images on large data bases</article-title><source><italic>Magnetic Resonance Imaging</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>19</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>73</fpage><lpage>88</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11295349</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Metaxas</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A hybrid framework for 3D medical image segmentation</article-title><source><italic>Medical Image Analysis</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>9</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>547</fpage><lpage>565</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15896997</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="fig1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>CC structure and partition of the CC boundary (image modified based onoriginal illustration from [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B5">3</xref>]).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2007-24826.001"/></fig><fig id="fig2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Illustration of the seed initialization process. (a) User-initializedpolyline. (b) Point tracing. (c) Completed seed contour.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2007-24826.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>An example of the initialized seed. (a) User-initialized polyline. (b) Theedge map. (c) The completed seed contour.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2007-24826.003"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Flow chart of the fornixremoval algorithm.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2007-24826.004"/></fig><fig id="fig5" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>(a) Distinct points aroundthe fornix. (b) The example of disconnected fornix. (c) The result withoutfornix removal. (d) The result with fornix removal.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2007-24826.005"/></fig><fig id="fig6" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>(a) The seed contour initializedby the user. (b) The fornix begins to appear without fornix removal. (c) Theresults with fornix removal. (d) The results overlaid on the edge map.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2007-24826.006"/></fig><fig id="fig7" position="float"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>(a) The seed contour initializedby the user. (b) The fornix begins to appear without fornix removal. (c) Theresults with fornix removal. (d) The results overlaid on the edge map.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2007-24826.007"/></fig><fig id="fig8" position="float"><label>Figure 8</label><caption><p>(a) The portion between two circles is outside. (b) The seed notcovering the fornix.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2007-24826.008"/></fig><table-wrap id="tab1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Quantitative validation results.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">FNF</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">FPF</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">TPF</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Dice</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">overlap</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mean</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0689</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0613</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.9525</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.9364</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.8803</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Std</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0613</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0401</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0438</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0178</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0304</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>